WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.159
Stage seven: anatomy of a run.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.723
Sunday: eighteen kilometers, eight hundred twenty meters of climbing.

3
00:00:09.823 --> 00:00:18.564
The MCP server times out on FIT files, so the skill downloads them locally, no password needed. One measurement per second.

4
00:00:19.414 --> 00:00:22.096
Time spent in each heart rate zone.

5
00:00:22.196 --> 00:00:29.059
And pace adjusted for grade, which flattens the climbs so an uphill can be compared to flat ground.

6
00:00:29.909 --> 00:00:35.684
Aerobic decoupling compares first-half efficiency with second-half efficiency.

7
00:00:35.784 --> 00:00:41.581
Here, three point eight percent: under the five percent marker. A marker, not a norm.

8
00:00:42.431 --> 00:00:46.350
Three climbs detected, each with its vertical speed.

9
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:49.666
And downhill, efficiency by grade class.

10
00:00:51.431 --> 00:00:55.500
Durability: the last third of the run, compared with the first.

11
00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.522
Then heart rate recovery, read against comparable efforts, never alone.

12
00:01:01.431 --> 00:01:06.780
Two calorie figures: Garmin, which stays the reference, and an independent model.

13
00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:10.778
Beyond fifteen percent apart, a flag. Here, four.

14
00:01:11.628 --> 00:01:18.534
For hill reps or strides, the analysis isolates every repetition: pace, heart rate, cadence.

15
00:01:20.628 --> 00:01:26.873
Same course, three runs: the comparison recognizes the climbs and shows the progress.

16
00:01:26.973 --> 00:01:29.612
Twelve minutes faster since June.

17
00:01:32.328 --> 00:01:37.101
To go further: the “Session analysis” page of the documentation.
